"""A geopolitical switching-cost schedule from UN General Assembly ideal points (Bailey, Strezhnev & Voeten; un-project.org API,
re-centred per year), 2019-2023 means. s_r = max(0, x_EU - x_r): the one-sided distance below the EU on the liberal-order axis
(regions on the Western side of the EU - US, UK, Canada, Australia - carry no political cost of aligning with an EU-led club).
g_r = 0.5 + s_r / (2 s_med): 0.5 for s = 0, 1 at the median distance, 2 at three times the median. Thresholds: trade x g (symmetric),
or join = trade x g and leave = trade / g (asymmetric: alignment lowers the entry cost and raises the exit cost)."""
